    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0337" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.911/9–2547</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Argentina </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 43</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-08">October 8,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State transmits the enclosed letter from Secretary of Defense
                    Forrestal to Dr. Gainza Paz, congratulating him on the 78th anniversary of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi><anchor n="47" xml:id="d269-f1"/> The
                    Officer in Charge of Mission is requested to forward this letter to Dr. Gainza
                    Paz if he transmitted Secretary Marshall’s message contained in the Department’s
                    telegram No. 921 of October 1, 1947. If the Officer in Charge did not forward
                    Secretary Marshall’s message or if he deems it in any way inappropriate to
                    transmit Mr. Forrestal’s letter, he will please notify the Department to this
                    effect.</p>
                <p>The letter from the Secretary of Defense was sealed upon its arrival in the
                    Department. An officer of the Department has been informed, however, that it
                    reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dear Dr. Paz:</p>
                        <p>Please accept my warm congratulations on the 78th anniversary of <hi
                                rendition="#italic">La Prensa. La Prensa</hi> has every reason to be
                            proud of the high journalistic standards to which it has consistently
                            adhered. I am confident that in the years to come these standards will
                            be maintained and <hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi> will continue
                            to champion enlightenment and international understanding.</p>
                        <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">James Forrestal”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d269-f1" n="47" xml:id="d269-f1-content">
                <p>The Department, in telegram 952, October 8, transmitted similar congratulations
                    from the Secretary of Agriculture (835.911/10–847).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
